},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Structural Biology Brussels, Vrije Universiteit Brussels, Brussels, Belgium."}]}},{"fullName":"Molina H","firstName":"Henrik","lastName":"Molina","initials":"H","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Proteomics Resource Center, The Rockefeller University, New York, NY, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Yu Z","firstName":"Zhiheng","lastName":"Yu","initials":"Z","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Howard Hughes Medical Institute, Janelia Research Campus, Ashburn, VA, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"des Georges A","firstName":"Amedee","lastName":"des Georges","initials":"A","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9704-3781"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Structural Biology Initiative, CUNY Advanced Science Research Center, New York, NY, USA. adesgeorges@gc.cuny.edu."},{"affiliation":"Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry, City College of New York, New York, NY, USA. adesgeorges@gc.cuny.edu."},{"affiliation":"Biochemistry and Chemistry PhD Programs, Graduate Center, City University of New York, New York, NY, USA. adesgeorges@gc.cuny.edu."}]}},{"fullName":"Lefkowitz RJ","firstName":"Robert J","lastName":"Lefkowitz","initials":"RJ","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1472-7545"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Medicine, Duke University Medical Center, Durham, NC, USA. lefko001@receptor-biol.duke.edu."},{"affiliation":"Department of Biochemistry, Duke University Medical Center, Durham, NC, USA. lefko001@receptor-biol.duke.edu."},{"affiliation":"Howard Hughes Medical Institute, Duke University Medical Center, Durham, NC, USA. lefko001@receptor-biol.duke.edu."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6656-6320"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9124-5414"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3825-874X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5189-5647"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6079-3992"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7174-9161"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8210-3446"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9704-3781"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1472-7545"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1638-8911"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1702-8619"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2034-2684"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4295-1229"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0001-8904-9972"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data","protocols","recommended_reviews","related_data","wikipedia"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"12","volume":"26","journalIssueId":2889974,"dateOfPublication":"2019 Dec","monthOfPublication":12,"yearOfPublication":2019,"printPublicationDate":"2019-12-01","journal":{"title":"Nature structural & molecular biology","medlineAbbreviation":"Nat Struct Mol Biol","isoabbreviation":"Nat Struct Mol Biol","essn":"1545-9985","issn":"1545-9993","nlmid":"101186374"}},"pubYear":"2019","pageInfo":"1123-1131","abstractText":"Classically, G-protein-coupled receptors (GPCRs) are thought to activate G protein from the plasma membrane and are subsequently desensitized by β-arrestin (β-arr). However, some GPCRs continue to signal through G protein from internalized compartments, mediated by a GPCR-G protein-β-arr 'megaplex'. Nevertheless, the molecular architecture of the megaplex remains unknown. Here, we present its cryo-electron microscopy structure, which shows simultaneous engagement of human G protein and bovine β-arr to the core and phosphorylated tail, respectively, of a single active human chimeric β<sub>2</sub>-adrenergic receptor with the C-terminal tail of the arginine vasopressin type 2 receptor (β<sub>2</sub>V<sub>2</sub>R). All three components adopt their canonical active conformations, suggesting that a single megaplex GPCR is capable of simultaneously activating G protein and β-arr. Our findings provide a structural basis for GPCR-mediated sustained internalized G protein signaling.","affiliation":"Department of Medicine, Duke University Medical Center, Durham, NC, USA.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Journal Article","Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"grantId":"F30 HL149213","agency":"NHLBI NIH HHS","acronym":"HL","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"P41 GM103310","agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"R01 HL016037","agency":"NHLBI NIH HHS","acronym":"HL","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"R35 GM133598","agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"S10 OD019994","agency":"NIH HHS","acronym":"OD","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"T32 GM007171","agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"T32 GM007767","agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"F30 HL129803","agency":"NHLBI NIH HHS","acronym":"HL","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"P41 RR001209","agency":"NCRR NIH HHS","acronym":"RR","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"R172-2014-1468","agency":"Lundbeck Foundation","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Endosomes","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cattle"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"GTP-Binding Proteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"Y"},{"abbreviation":"UL","qualifierName":"ultrastructure","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Receptors, G-Protein-Coupled","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"Y"},{"abbreviation":"UL","qualifierName":"ultrastructure","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Receptors, Adrenergic, beta-2","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"UL","qualifierName":"ultrastructure","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Receptors, Vasopressin","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"UL","qualifierName":"ultrastructure","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cryoelectron Microscopy"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Signal Transduction"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Protein Conformation"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Models, Molecular"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"beta-Arrestins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"Y"},{"abbreviation":"UL","qualifierName":"ultrastructure","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}}]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"GTP-Binding Proteins","registryNumber":"EC 3.6.1.-"},{"name":"Receptors, Vasopressin","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Receptors, G-Protein-Coupled","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Receptors, Adrenergic, beta-2","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"beta-Arrestins","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"AVPR2 protein, human","registryNumber":"0"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Free","availabilityCode":"F","documentStyle":"html","site":"Unpaywall","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/7108872"},{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41594-019-0330-y"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC7108872"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC7108872?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"Y","citedByCount":194,"hasData":"Y","hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"Y","dbCrossReferenceList":{"dbName":["PRIDE"]},"hasLabsLinks":"Y","hasEvaluations":"N","authMan":"Y","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"Y","manuscriptId":"NIHMS1541120","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["emdb","pxd","pdb"]},"dateOfCompletion":"2020-02-25","dateOfCreation":"2019-11-20","firstIndexDate":"2019-11-20","fullTextReceivedDate":"2025-02-03","dateOfRevision":"2023-01-20","electronicPublicationDate":"2019-11-18","firstPublicationDate":"2019-11-18","embargoDate":"2020-05-18"},{"id":"PPR811082","source":"PPR","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PPR811082"]},"doi":"10.1101/2024.02.21.581355","title":"A genetically-encoded nanobody sensor reveals conformational diversity in β-arrestins orchestrated by distinct seven transmembrane receptors","authorString":"Sarma P, Marková VN, Zaidi N, Dalal A, Mishra S, Yadav MK, Mahajan G, Roy N, Miclea P, Lazar J, Shukla AK.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Sarma P","firstName":"Parishmita","lastName":"Sarma","initials":"P","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences and Bioengineering, Indian Institute of Technology, Kanpur 208016, India"}]}},{"fullName":"Marková VN","firstName":"Vendula Nagy","lastName":"Marková","initials":"VN","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"First Faculty of Medicine, Charles University in Prague, Kateřinská 32, 121 08 Prague"},{"affiliation":"Institute of Organic Chemistry and Biochemistry CAS, Flemingovo nám. 2, 160 00 Prague"},{"affiliation":"Faculty of Science, Charles University in Prague, Albertov 6, 128 00 Prague, Czech Republic"}]}},{"fullName":"Zaidi N","firstName":"Nashrah","lastName":"Zaidi","initials":"N","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences and Bioengineering, Indian Institute of Technology, Kanpur 208016, India"}]}},{"fullName":"Dalal A","firstName":"Annu","lastName":"Dalal","initials":"A","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0002-1762-7339"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences and Bioengineering, Indian Institute of Technology, Kanpur 208016, India"}]}},{"fullName":"Mishra S","firstName":"Sudha","lastName":"Mishra","initials":"S","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences and Bioengineering, Indian Institute of Technology, Kanpur 208016, India"}]}},{"fullName":"Yadav MK","firstName":"Manish","lastName":"Yadav","initials":"MK","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4297-7779"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences and Bioengineering, Indian Institute of Technology, Kanpur 208016, India"}]}},{"fullName":"Mahajan G","firstName":"Gargi","lastName":"Mahajan","initials":"G","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences and Bioengineering, Indian Institute of Technology, Kanpur 208016, India"}]}},{"fullName":"Roy N","firstName":"Nabarun","lastName":"Roy","initials":"N","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences and Bioengineering, Indian Institute of Technology, Kanpur 208016, India"}]}},{"fullName":"Miclea P","firstName":"Paul","lastName":"Miclea","initials":"P","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"First Faculty of Medicine, Charles University in Prague, Kateřinská 32, 121 08 Prague"},{"affiliation":"Institute of Organic Chemistry and Biochemistry CAS, Flemingovo nám. 2, 160 00 Prague"}]}},{"fullName":"Lazar J","firstName":"Josef","lastName":"Lazar","initials":"J","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6285-3995"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"First Faculty of Medicine, Charles University in Prague, Kateřinská 32, 121 08 Prague"},{"affiliation":"Institute of Organic Chemistry and Biochemistry CAS, Flemingovo nám. 2, 160 00 Prague"}]}},{"fullName":"Shukla AK","firstName":"Arun","lastName":"Shukla","initials":"AK","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences and Bioengineering, Indian Institute of Technology, Kanpur 208016, India"}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6285-3995"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4297-7779"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0002-1762-7339"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data"]},"pubYear":"2024","abstractText":"Agonist-induced interaction of G protein-coupled receptors (GPCRs) with β-arrestins (βarrs) is a critical mechanism that regulates the spatio-temporal pattern of receptor localization and downstream signaling. While the underlying mechanism governing GPCR-βarr interaction is primarily conserved and involves receptor activation and phosphorylation, there are several examples of receptor-specific fine-tuning of βarr-mediated functional outcomes. Considering the key contribution of conformational plasticity of βarrs in driving receptor-specific functional responses, it is important to develop and characterize novel sensors capable of reporting distinct βarr conformations in cellular context. Here, we design an intrabody version of a βarr-recognizing nanobody (nanobody32), referred to as intrabody32 (Ib32), in NanoLuc enzyme complementation assay format, and measure its ability to recognize βarr1 and 2 in live cells upon activation of a broad set of GPCRs. We discover that Ib32 robustly recognizes activated βarr1 and 2 in the plasma membrane as well as in the endosomes, and effectively mirrors βarr recruitment profile upon stimulation of GPCRs. We also design an Ib32 sensor for single-photon polarization microscopy with a change in linear dichroism as readout and demonstrate its utility for monitoring βarr activation upon stimulation of angiotensin receptor by its natural and biased agonists. Interestingly, when used side-by-side with a previously described sensor of βarr1 conformation known as Ib30, Ib32 uncovers distinct conformational signatures imparted on βarrs by different GPCRs, which is further corroborated using an orthogonal limited proteolysis assay. Taken together, our study presents Ib32 as a novel sensor to monitor βarr activation and leverages it to uncover conformational diversity encoded in the GPCR-βarr system with direct implications for improving the current understanding of GPCR signaling and regulatory paradigms.","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Preprint"]},"bookOrReportDetails":{"publisher":"bioRxiv","yearOfPublication":2024},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"doi","site":"Unpaywall","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2024.02.21.581355"},{"availability":"Free","availabilityCode":"F","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2024.02.21.581355"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/article/PPR/PPR811082"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/api/fulltextRepo?pprId=PPR811082&type=FILE&fileName=EMS194427-pdf.pdf&mimeType=application/pdf"}]},"commentCorrectionList":{"commentCorrection":[{"id":"40924451","source":"MED","reference":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America. 2025 Sep;122(37):e2507384122","type":"Preprint of","note":"CrossRef Pre-print loader","orderIn":10001}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"Y","citedByCount":0,"hasData":"Y","hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasLabsLinks":"Y","license":"cc by-nc-nd","hasEvaluations":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"Y","nihAuthMan":"N","manuscriptId":"EMS194427","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["pdb","doi"]},"dateOfCreation":"2024-02-28","firstIndexDate":"2024-02-28","fullTextReceivedDate":"2024-03-21","firstPublicationDate":"2024-02-22"},{"id":"35677880","source":"MED","pmid":"35677880","pmcid":"PMC9170359","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC9170359"]},"doi":"10.3389/fmolb.2022.863099","title":"Accelerating GPCR Drug Discovery With Conformation-Stabilizing VHHs.","authorString":"Laeremans T, Sands ZA, Claes P, De Blieck A, De Cesco S, Triest S, Busch A, Felix D, Kumar A, Jaakola VP, Menet C.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Laeremans T","firstName":"Toon","lastName":"Laeremans","initials":"T","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Confo Therapeutics NV, Zwijnaarde, Belgium."}]}},{"fullName":"Sands ZA","firstName":"Zara A","lastName":"Sands","initials":"ZA","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Confo Therapeutics NV, Zwijnaarde, Belgium."}]}},{"fullName":"Claes P","firstName":"Pieter","lastName":"Claes","initials":"P","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Confo Therapeutics NV, Zwijnaarde, Belgium."}]}},{"fullName":"De Blieck A","firstName":"Ann","lastName":"De Blieck","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Confo Therapeutics NV, Zwijnaarde, Belgium."}]}},{"fullName":"De Cesco S","firstName":"Stephane","lastName":"De Cesco","initials":"S","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4443-4217"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Confo Therapeutics NV, Zwijnaarde, Belgium."}]}},{"fullName":"Triest S","firstName":"Sarah","lastName":"Triest","initials":"S","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0001-8904-9972"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Confo Therapeutics NV, Zwijnaarde, Belgium."}]}},{"fullName":"Busch A","firstName":"Andreas","lastName":"Busch","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Confo Therapeutics NV, Zwijnaarde, Belgium."}]}},{"fullName":"Felix D","firstName":"David","lastName":"Felix","initials":"D","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Confo Therapeutics NV, Zwijnaarde, Belgium."}]}},{"fullName":"Kumar A","firstName":"Abhinav","lastName":"Kumar","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Confo Therapeutics NV, Zwijnaarde, Belgium."}]}},{"fullName":"Jaakola VP","firstName":"Veli-Pekka","lastName":"Jaakola","initials":"VP","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Confo Therapeutics NV, Zwijnaarde, Belgium."}]}},{"fullName":"Menet C","firstName":"Christel","lastName":"Menet","initials":"C","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Confo Therapeutics NV, Zwijnaarde, Belgium."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4443-4217"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0001-8904-9972"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"volume":"9","journalIssueId":3307029,"dateOfPublication":"2022 ","monthOfPublication":0,"yearOfPublication":2022,"printPublicationDate":"2022-01-01","journal":{"title":"Frontiers in molecular biosciences","medlineAbbreviation":"Front Mol Biosci","isoabbreviation":"Front Mol Biosci","essn":"2296-889X","issn":"2296-889X","nlmid":"101653173"}},"pubYear":"2022","pageInfo":"863099","abstractText":"The human genome encodes 850 G protein-coupled receptors (GPCRs), half of which are considered potential drug targets. GPCRs transduce extracellular stimuli into a plethora of vital physiological processes. Consequently, GPCRs are an attractive drug target class. This is underlined by the fact that approximately 40% of marketed drugs modulate GPCRs. Intriguingly 60% of non-olfactory GPCRs have no drugs or candidates in clinical development, highlighting the continued potential of GPCRs as drug targets. The discovery of small molecules targeting these GPCRs by conventional high throughput screening (HTS) campaigns is challenging. Although the definition of success varies per company, the success rate of HTS for GPCRs is low compared to other target families (Fujioka and Omori, 2012; Dragovich et al., 2022). Beyond this, GPCR structure determination can be difficult, which often precludes the application of structure-based drug design approaches to arising HTS hits. GPCR structural studies entail the resource-demanding purification of native receptors, which can be challenging as they are inherently unstable when extracted from the lipid matrix. Moreover, GPCRs are flexible molecules that adopt distinct conformations, some of which need to be stabilized if they are to be structurally resolved. The complexity of targeting distinct therapeutically relevant GPCR conformations during the early discovery stages contributes to the high attrition rates for GPCR drug discovery programs. Multiple strategies have been explored in an attempt to stabilize GPCRs in distinct conformations to better understand their pharmacology. This review will focus on the use of camelid-derived immunoglobulin single variable domains (VHHs) that stabilize disease-relevant pharmacological states (termed ConfoBodies by the authors) of GPCRs, as well as GPCR:signal transducer complexes, to accelerate drug discovery. These VHHs are powerful tools for supporting in vitro screening, deconvolution of complex GPCR pharmacology, and structural biology purposes. In order to demonstrate the potential impact of ConfoBodies on translational research, examples are presented of their role in active state screening campaigns and structure-informed rational design to identify <i>de novo</i> chemical space and, subsequently, how such matter can be elaborated into more potent and selective drug candidates with intended pharmacology.","affiliation":"Confo Therapeutics NV, Zwijnaarde, Belgium.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic-eCollection","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["review-article","Review","Journal Article"]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Biosensor","conformation","Gpcr","Sbdd","Active State","Vhh","Conformer","Confobody"]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmolb.2022.863099"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC9170359"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC9170359?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"Y","citedByCount":39,"hasData":"Y","hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasLabsLinks":"Y","license":"cc by","hasEvaluations":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["gen","pdb"]},"dateOfCreation":"2022-06-09","firstIndexDate":"2022-06-10","fullTextReceivedDate":"2025-02-02","dateOfRevision":"2022-07-16","electronicPublicationDate":"2022-05-23","firstPublicationDate":"2022-05-23"},{"id":"37558880","source":"MED","pmid":"37558880","pmcid":"PMC10447241","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC10447241"]},"doi":"10.1038/s41586-023-06420-x","title":"Tail engagement of arrestin at the glucagon receptor.","authorString":"Chen K, Zhang C, Lin S, Yan X, Cai H, Yi C, Ma L, Chu X, Liu Y, Zhu Y, Han S, Zhao Q, Wu B.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Chen K","firstName":"Kun","lastName":"Chen","initials":"K","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7727-2384"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Drug Research, State Key Laboratory of Chemical Biology, Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai, China."},{"affiliation":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Zhang C","firstName":"Chenhui","lastName":"Zhang","initials":"C","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Drug Research, State Key Laboratory of Chemical Biology, Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai, China."},{"affiliation":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Lin S","firstName":"Shuling","lastName":"Lin","initials":"S","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0002-3932-6414"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Drug Research, State Key Laboratory of Chemical Biology, Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Yan X","firstName":"Xinyu","lastName":"Yan","initials":"X","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Chinese Materia Medica, Nanjing University of Chinese Medicine, Nanjing, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Cai H","firstName":"Heng","lastName":"Cai","initials":"H","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Pharmaceutical Science and Technology, Hangzhou Institute for Advanced Study, University of Chinese Academy of Sciences, Hangzhou, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Yi C","firstName":"Cuiying","lastName":"Yi","initials":"C","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Drug Research, State Key Laboratory of Chemical Biology, Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Ma L","firstName":"Limin","lastName":"Ma","initials":"L","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Drug Research, State Key Laboratory of Chemical Biology, Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Chu X","firstName":"Xiaojing","lastName":"Chu","initials":"X","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Drug Research, State Key Laboratory of Chemical Biology, Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Liu Y","firstName":"Yuchen","lastName":"Liu","initials":"Y","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Drug Research, State Key Laboratory of Chemical Biology, Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai, China."},{"affiliation":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Zhu Y","firstName":"Ya","lastName":"Zhu","initials":"Y","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Lingang Laboratory, Shanghai, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Han S","firstName":"Shuo","lastName":"Han","initials":"S","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Drug Research, State Key Laboratory of Chemical Biology, Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai, China."},{"affiliation":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing, China."},{"affiliation":"School of Pharmaceutical Science and Technology, Hangzhou Institute for Advanced Study, University of Chinese Academy of Sciences, Hangzhou, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Zhao Q","firstName":"Qiang","lastName":"Zhao","initials":"Q","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6251-6676"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Drug Research, State Key Laboratory of Chemical Biology, Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai, China. zhaoq@simm.ac.cn."},{"affiliation":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing, China. zhaoq@simm.ac.cn."},{"affiliation":"School of Chinese Materia Medica, Nanjing University of Chinese Medicine, Nanjing, China. zhaoq@simm.ac.cn."},{"affiliation":"Zhongshan Institute for Drug Discovery, Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Zhongshan, China. zhaoq@simm.ac.cn."}]}},{"fullName":"Wu B","firstName":"Beili","lastName":"Wu","initials":"B","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1936-0909"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Drug Research, State Key Laboratory of Chemical Biology, Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai, China. beiliwu@simm.ac.cn."},{"affiliation":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing, China. beiliwu@simm.ac.cn."},{"affiliation":"School of Pharmaceutical Science and Technology, Hangzhou Institute for Advanced Study, University of Chinese Academy of Sciences, Hangzhou, China. beiliwu@simm.ac.cn."},{"affiliation":"School of Life Science and Technology, ShanghaiTech University, Shanghai, China. beiliwu@simm.ac.cn."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6251-6676"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1936-0909"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7727-2384"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0002-3932-6414"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data","related_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"7975","volume":"620","journalIssueId":3617962,"dateOfPublication":"2023 Aug","monthOfPublication":8,"yearOfPublication":2023,"printPublicationDate":"2023-08-01","journal":{"title":"Nature","medlineAbbreviation":"Nature","isoabbreviation":"Nature","essn":"1476-4687","issn":"0028-0836","nlmid":"0410462"}},"pubYear":"2023","pageInfo":"904-910","abstractText":"Arrestins have pivotal roles in regulating G protein-coupled receptor (GPCR) signalling by desensitizing G protein activation and mediating receptor internalization<sup>1,2</sup>. It has been proposed that the arrestin binds to the receptor in two different conformations, 'tail' and 'core', which were suggested to govern distinct processes of receptor signalling and trafficking<sup>3,4</sup>. However, little structural information is available for the tail engagement of the arrestins. Here we report two structures of the glucagon receptor (GCGR) bound to β-arrestin 1 (βarr1) in glucagon-bound and ligand-free states. These structures reveal a receptor tail-engaged binding mode of βarr1 with many unique features, to our knowledge, not previously observed. Helix VIII, instead of the receptor core, has a major role in accommodating βarr1 by forming extensive interactions with the central crest of βarr1. The tail-binding pose is further defined by a close proximity between the βarr1 C-edge and the receptor helical bundle, and stabilized by a phosphoinositide derivative that bridges βarr1 with helices I and VIII of GCGR. Lacking any contact with the arrestin, the receptor core is in an inactive state and loosely binds to glucagon. Further functional studies suggest that the tail conformation of GCGR-βarr governs βarr recruitment at the plasma membrane and endocytosis of GCGR, and provides a molecular basis for the receptor forming a super-complex simultaneously with G protein and βarr to promote sustained signalling within endosomes. These findings extend our knowledge about the arrestin-mediated modulation of GPCR functionalities.","affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Drug Research, State Key Laboratory of Chemical Biology, Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai, China.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cell Membrane","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Endosomes","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Glucagon","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Heterotrimeric GTP-Binding Proteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Phosphatidylinositols","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Receptors, Glucagon","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Ligands"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Endocytosis"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Protein Binding"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"beta-Arrestin 1","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}}]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"Glucagon","registryNumber":"9007-92-5"},{"name":"Phosphatidylinositols","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Ligands","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Receptors, Glucagon","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"Heterotrimeric GTP-Binding Proteins","registryNumber":"EC 3.6.5.1"},{"name":"beta-Arrestin 1","registryNumber":"0"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Unpaywall","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06420-x.pdf"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Unpaywall","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06420-x.pdf"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Unpaywall","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06420-x.pdf"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Unpaywall","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06420-x.pdf"},{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06420-x"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC10447241"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC10447241?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"Y","citedByCount":70,"hasData":"Y","hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"Y","dbCrossReferenceList":{"dbName":["PDB"]},"hasLabsLinks":"Y","license":"cc by","hasEvaluations":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["pdb"]},"dateOfCompletion":"2023-08-26","dateOfCreation":"2023-08-09","firstIndexDate":"2023-08-11","fullTextReceivedDate":"2025-02-03","dateOfRevision":"2025-09-24","electronicPublicationDate":"2023-08-09","firstPublication